---------------------- ROTOR-TEETER --------------------------------------------
          0   TeetMod     - Rotor-teeter spring/damper model {0: none, 1: standard, 2: user-defined from routine UserTeet} (switch) [unused for 3 blades]
          0   TeetDmpP    - Rotor-teeter damper position (degrees) [used only for 2 blades and when TeetMod=1]
          0   TeetDmp     - Rotor-teeter damping constant (N-m/(rad/s)) [used only for 2 blades and when TeetMod=1]
          0   TeetCDmp    - Rotor-teeter rate-independent Coulomb-damping moment (N-m) [used only for 2 blades and when TeetMod=1]
          0   TeetSStP    - Rotor-teeter soft-stop position (degrees) [used only for 2 blades and when TeetMod=1]
          0   TeetHStP    - Rotor-teeter hard-stop position (degrees) [used only for 2 blades and when TeetMod=1]
          0   TeetSSSp    - Rotor-teeter soft-stop linear-spring constant (N-m/rad) [used only for 2 blades and when TeetMod=1]
          0   TeetHSSp    - Rotor-teeter hard-stop linear-spring constant (N-m/rad) [used only for 2 blades and when TeetMod=1]
---------------------- DRIVETRAIN ----------------------------------------------
       92.8   GBoxEff    - Obtained by taking the average of all the efficiencies using T3.9 (see Excel Sheet GearBox) - Gearbox efficiency (%)
      90.84   GBRatio    - T3.8 - NOTE: 91 in WTC3 file - Gearbox ratio (-)
  5.5465+08   DTTorSpr   - Equal to G.Kt / L, where the product  G.Kt is the average of G*Ip over the shaft using values from T3.3 (see Excel Sheet Shaft) - Drivetrain torsional spring (N-m/rad)
  5.5465+05   DTTorDmp   - TODO Using value stiffeness proportionality constant 0.001 from Tab3.5 and multiplying it to DTTTorSpr - Drivetrain torsional damper (N-m/(rad/s))
